# core.files' FileReader and FileWriter, core.term's binary cursor
# (`Reader.over`) and standard input implement the Prelude Reader and
# Writer. One generic `drain` reads each to its end through `read_into`, and
# one generic `pipe` copies a file into a FileWriter through `read_bytes`,
# `write_bytes` and `flush`. The cursor and standard input also read through
# their own `read_bytes`, `read` and `read_into`, and FileWriter writes
# through `write_bytes` and its own `write_all`, called on the named type.
# The cursor refuses a zero limit. Each tier prints the same lines.
fixture: CoreByteSourcesMeetThePreludeReaderAndWriter.fixture
env: NO_COLOR=1
step: jet check run.jet
exit: 0
step: jet run -O0 run.jet
stdin: input.stdin
exit: 0
stdout: = core_byte_sources_meet_the_prelude_reader_and_writer.out
step: jet run -O1 run.jet
stdin: input.stdin
exit: 0
stdout: = core_byte_sources_meet_the_prelude_reader_and_writer.out
step: jet run -O2 run.jet
stdin: input.stdin
exit: 0
stdout: = core_byte_sources_meet_the_prelude_reader_and_writer.out
